"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\ngenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\nclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\nD20 (Loaded Later, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\"; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary DEX and recover\nthe module contract\"): 7-entry APK with `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain dex 035); NEW codec `dynamic` whose `data` is\nthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\nin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\nD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\nwhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\nNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\nAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD22 (Root of Trust, `root_detection` \"synthetic root detection\"; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals\nwithout globally patching success\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec `base64` (4th time), debuggable false again. No root\nprobe API (File/Build/Runtime.exec/su/magisk) in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `rootSignals` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nFIRST 6-set Mastery (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22 base64).\nD23 (Hook Line and Signal, `hook_detection` \"hook and instrumentation detection\"; prompt \"Separate real instrumentation\nsignals from generated false positives\"): single = v1 `xor` (key 81). **TT and all 7 Mastery sets (d02, d06, d10, d14,\nd15, d22, d23 -- old days REGENERATED) shipped puzzle schema v2 `{\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..}` with NO data: the answer\nis COMPUTED by dex code** -- `Release.code(Context)` = `\"ANS-\"` + 16 hex nibbles of a static 64-bit mixer chain\n(`token()` = mixA(scanB(mixC(seed))); `scan*` folds in `Probe.s1/s2/s3` 12-bit inverse searches and a theme gate fn such\nas `instrumentationSignals = (a^b^c)&7`; d14 set adds an LCG `long[16]` table walk; d15 set calls JNI `nativeShare(long)`\nin `libarena.so`). Unreferenced look-alike mixers/`K*` consts = the \"generated false positives\". Solved by jadx +\njavac-with-Context-stub (LLM worker); the solver had no v2 path and `bytecode_vm_scan` resolved 2 of 8 v2 APKs.\nD24 (Emulator Alibi, `emulator_detection` \"emulator environment detection\"; prompt \"Defeat app-owned environment checks on\nthe same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle\"): single = v1 `split` (`parts[3]` + `order [2,0,1]`). TT + FIRST 8-set\nMastery (d03, d06, d09, d10, d15, d17, d23, d24) all v2 `analysis`, same shape as D23: theme = gate fn\n`EmulatorAlibi.emulatorScore(a,b,c) = (a+b+c)%4` over `Probe.s*` ints, decoys `sealEmu*`/`KQemu*`; NO Build/qemu/sensor/\ntelephony API in any dex. The overnight v2 evaluator (lib deep Dalvik eval + solve.py unicorn JNI hop) solved all three\nmodes first try (single 16.3 s via race probe, TT 2.5 s, Mastery 3.1 s).\nD25 (Integrity Signals, `integrity_signal` \"challenge-owned integrity statement\"; prompt \"Forge or replay a bounded\nchallenge-owned integrity statement and explain the missing binding\" -- Play Integrity nonce/requestHash pun): single =\nv1 `hex`. TT = v2 with gate `IntegritySignals.integrityStatement(long,int) = a ^ (long)b` (first `(JI)J` gate; only 2\nprobe calls), classes `SealCheck`/`VerdictMap`, decoys `KSeal*`/`KStatement*`/`KCert*`; NO PackageManager/signature/\nIntegrityManager/token code. FIRST 9-set Mastery (d01, d04, d07, d10, d14, d16, d19, d22, d25), all v2, and the old-day\nsets now carry their REAL mechanic: d19 set = `Class.forName`/`getDeclaredMethod`/`Method.invoke` dispatch picking 1 of\n8 `Maze.mN(long)` via a packed-switch `dispatch(int)`; d16 set = `native nativeShare(long,int)` with the u16\nlength-narrowing gate in the export. Solver 3/3 first try (single ~5 s race probe, TT 2.2 s, Mastery 3.7 s; Mastery solve\n1.89 s, double D24's).\nD26 (Split Decision, `split_apk` \"base and feature split correlation\"; prompt \"Reassemble evidence distributed across base\nand configuration splits\"): FIRST non-APK container in all modes -- `*.apks` = stored zip of `base.apk` + `feature.apk`\n(manifest `split=\"arena_feature\"`, `hasCode=false`, one asset). Single v1: base `split` puzzle with an EMPTY `parts` slot\nfilled from the feature's `huntress_feature.json` `{part, part_index}`, then `r[order[i]]=parts[i]`. TT + Mastery set10\nv2: gate `SplitDecision.splitIndex(a,b)=(a<<4)|b`, and the FIRST chain that READS ARTIFACT BYTES: `Assets.readSplit\n(\"huntress_feature.bin\")` walks `getApplicationInfo().splitSourceDirs` with `java.util.zip.ZipFile`, reads 16 B, folds\ntwo big-endian u64 into the token. The deep evaluator aborted (no split bytes) -> solver silent in TT and on set10; live\nworkers hand-solved (TT 83 s, Mastery 88 s). 10-set Mastery: old-day d11/d13/d21 first time as v2, pure chains.\nD27 (Dependency Surface, `legacy_dependency` \"reachable challenge-owned dependency\"; prompt \"Prove which generated\ndependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface\" -- MASVS-CODE-3 / SCA reachability): **full DE-ESCALATION**.\nSingle AND TT = plain 6-entry v1 fixture, codec `base64`; TT dex back to the D17-D22 shape (tag dropped, `STRUCTURAL`, stub\n`DependencySurface.exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`, never called); no library code, no extra dex.\nFIRST 11-set Mastery and ALL 11 v1 (d01 d04 d07 d10+NSC d11 d14 d18 d20+payload.dex d21 d26.apks d27), old days with\ntheir ORIGINAL codecs; the d26 set kept its `.apks` (v1 base + feature JSON fragment). Solver 3/3, no LLM work (single\n~6 s, TT 3.0 s, Mastery 3.4 s / solve 0.40 s). v2 is not retired: assume either schema per set, every day.\nD28 (Protocol Reconstruction, `binary_protocol` \"binary protocol framing\"; prompt \"Reconstruct the app-to-backend protocol\nand preserve nonce and ordering semantics\"): single = v1 with NEW codec `packet` (`data` = hex of one frame: magic `HA`,\nu8 length, ASCII answer, XOR checksum over all preceding bytes; solved by hex + `ANS-` search, no frame parser). v2 BACK\nin TT + all 12 Mastery sets: TT gate `frame(a,b,c)=(a<<16)|(b<<8)|c` inside a 7-round state-machine walk over two\n`int[8]` tables (round+1 = sequence; next state from the hash); no socket/ByteBuffer/CRC API, no `Probe`. Sets d01 d04\nd07 d08 d11 d14 d17 d18 d22 d24 d26.apks d28; first-time v2 d08 (pure), d17 (R8 `b->a`), d18 (real decrypt loop, FNV\nfold). Solver 3/3, no LLM work (single 3.2 s probe, TT 3.4 s, Mastery 2.9 s / solve 0.78 s).\nSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day; through D22 no exploit was ever needed. D23-D24 TT/Mastery\ncompute the answer in code: assume the timed builds evaluate code, and that tomorrow's theme becomes a gate\nfn / probe set INSIDE the v2 chain (the d10/d14/d22 sets already carry `gateDomain*`/`gateStream*` theme fns).\nD15-D22 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\nencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading -> anti-debug -> root detection -> hook (D23) -> emulator (D24) -> Play Integrity verdict (D25)).\nStill unnamed in that arc: tamper/repackaging/installer, key attestation (D22's title pun is\nthe attestation `RootOfTrust` ASN.1 record), certificate pinning checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box crypto). After it the untouched MASVS\ngroups are AUTH (biometric/local auth) and the leftover IPC surfaces (bound Service/AIDL, broadcast receivers).\nNext expect also: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\nmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\npinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\nbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\ncontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\ndynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor, d21 reverse): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D22+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.xml` | med (mixed Mastery) |\n| 5 | Custom permission weakness (normal level, typo, missing) | gap | manifest | `<permission protectionLevel=\"normal\">`, `android:permission` on comp vs `uses-permission` | `aapt dump permissions x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 6 | Task hijacking / StrandHogg | gap | manifest attrs (answer = static) | `taskAffinity`, `allowTaskReparenting=\"true\"`, `launchMode=\"singleTask\"` | `aapt dump xmltree ... \\| grep -E 'taskAffinity\\|launchMode\\|Reparent'` | med |\n| 7 | Tapjacking / overlay | gap | layout XML or manifest | `filterTouchesWhenObscured`, `FLAG_WINDOW_IS_OBSCURED`, `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | `apktool d` then `grep -r filterTouches out