or intent-filter); other libs' flaws are decoys.\n5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   Old-day v2 sets run their REAL mechanic: d19 forName(\"m\"+dispatch(k)).invoke -> only that Maze.mN; d16 (u16)len gate\n   -> the dex's own int arg; d18 decrypt loop; d17 a.b->a.a. D28 TT: int[8] next/val tables walked 7 rounds, keep order.\n5b. Split-reading chain (D26): base dex `readSplit(name)` walks ctx.getApplicationInfo().splitSourceDirs + ZipFile\n   getEntry(\"assets/\"+name) -> 16 B -> two big-endian u64 (`j=(j<<8)|(b[i]&255)`). Serve `unzip -p feature.apk\n   assets/<name>` to the port / javac stub. Split with hasCode=true -> jadx its dex too and javac all together.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23-D26 v2, D27 v1, D28 v2; 12 sets); each APK alone;\n   loop all answer_ids; one silent set -> hand-solve it, but batch-submit every answer in one request.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain,\nanalysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening, analysis-interface-signal-list-eval, analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs,\nanalysis-release-code-eval, analysis-self-integrity-stubs, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\nanti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload, apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbiometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, bundle-container-formats, cdex-vdex-string-pool,\ncert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs,\ncustom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel,\ndecrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-eval-float-double-semantics, dex-eval-java-random-lcg,\ndex-eval-long-intrinsics, dex-eval-native-bridge, dex-eval-pure-static-memo, dex-gated-branch-consts,\ndex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays,\ndispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-anchored-candidate-veto, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\nenum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table,\nhook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\ninstaller-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, instrumentation-false-positive-env, integrity-derived-key,\njanus-dex-apk-polyglot, java-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input,\njni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify, key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse,\nknown-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, kotlin-object-chain-eval,\nmastery-set-scaling-bench, messagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native,\nmulti-stage-loader-recurse, native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks, native-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt,\nnative-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate, native-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export,\nnative-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs, nested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch,\npayload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family,\npinned-emulator-env-profile, play-integrity-verdict-select, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields,\nr8-renamed-chain-follow, reflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve,\nrolling-xor-keystream-family, root-signal-vector-key, split-config-device-select, split-feature-dex-code,\nsplit-native-lib-config-abi, split-resources-arsc-overlay, split-signature-digest-binding, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt,\nstatic-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan,\nv1-manifest-digest-verify, v2-app-state-first-run-defaults, v2-debugger-gate-state-loop, v2-dexloader-payload-invoke,\nv2-reflection-api-breadth, v2-split-asset-read, v2-string-decrypt-name-resolve, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\n\nForecast after D27: D26's packaging turn did NOT continue -- D27 \"Dependency Surface\" (MASVS-CODE-3 software\ncomposition: \"which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface\") shipped NOTHING real: v1\n`base64` in single + TT, and all 11 Mastery sets went back to v1 with their original codecs (v2 absent after 4 days).\nSo (a) a TT/Mastery regeneration of D27 as v2 or as real bundled-library code is the likeliest near-term mutation\n(priority 1: dependency inventory, exported-surface -> lib-sink reachability, multidex, a `(ZI)I` gate fed by manifest\nfacts); (b) the MASVS-CODE group is now open: CODE-4 input validation (deep-link parse/allowlist bypass, zip slip in a\ndependency, deserialization), CODE-1 platform version gates, CODE-2 forced update (priority 2); (c) still unnamed for\nD28-D31 (4 days): certificate pinning, key attestation, tamper/repackaging, task hijacking/tapjacking, the obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and an all-days capstone. Mastery: 11 sets on D27 (+1/day -> ~15 by D31), schema\nper set unpredictable (v1 or v2); keep v1 decoders first in the race, v2 evaluator always armed. Old days not yet seen\nas v2: d05, d08, d12, d18, d20, d27.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"dependency-sbom-inventory\", \"concept\": \"bundled third-party dependency inventory (rows 106-108): library packages outside the app package, versions and their source\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 theme `legacy_dependency` / STRUCTURAL 'reachable challenge-owned dependency' shipped as words only; a regeneration will likely bundle 2+ generated libs. Pure-python `lib.android.dependency_inventory(apk) -> [{pkg, name, version, source, classes, dex}]`: group dex classes by package prefix not under the manifest package (and not android/androidx/kotlin/java), read version from `META-INF/*.version` (androidx style 'x.y.z'), `META-INF/maven/<g>/<a>/pom.properties` (version=), `META-INF/*.kotlin_module`, static final String fields named VERSION/VERSION_NAME/LIB_VERSION in the lib's BuildConfig, `assets/*.jar|*.aar` members (recurse), `lib/<abi>/*.so` version strings (`OpenSSL 1.0.1`, `SQLite 3.x`). Expose as a candidate feature for solve.py: values tied to a lib (ANS- consts, flaw ids like `HCTF-DEP-*`) are tagged with the lib. Regression: synthetic APK with 3 lib packages + pom.properties; D27 fixtures must still return []. Pure python, <0.1 s/APK.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"exported-surface-sink-reachability\", \"concept\": \"several generated dependency flaws; only the one reachable from a manifest-EXPORTED component counts (rows 1, 8, 106)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 prompt: 'Prove which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface'; TT stub `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`. Build on the existing entry-reachable-callgraph-rank, but start from EVERY exported component: parse the binary manifest for activity/activity-alias/service/receiver/provider with exported=true, or an intent-filter and no exported attr when targetSdk<31 (legacy implicit export), minus those guarded by a signature-level permission; entry methods onCreate/onNewIntent/onStartCommand/onBind/onReceive/query/insert/openFile/call/handleMessage. Walk invoke-static/virtual/direct/interface/super (+ reflection names already resolved by reflection-name-resolve, + Runnable/Handler/Thread.start edges) into lib packages; for each candidate value (ANS- const, flaw id, v2 Release-style chain) record reached/unreached; veto unreached ones in proof_flow ranking. Regression: synthetic APK with 3 libs x 1 flaw each, only one reached from an exported Activity, one from a non-exported Service (decoy), one dead.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v2-boolean-gate-manifest-facts\", \"concept\": \"v2 gate with boolean/narrow args fed by manifest/PackageManager facts (`(ZI)I` exportedReachability; ActivityInfo.exported, permission, targetSdk)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If D27 returns as v2 (TT mutation or Mastery regeneration), the gate is `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1` -- first boolean-typed theme arg. Deep evaluator: correct Z/B/S/C arg + return semantics (if-eqz on Z, int-to-byte/short/char narrowing, boolean returned as int), and intrinsics returning REAL manifest facts: PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_ACTIVITIES|GET_SERVICES|GET_RECEIVERS|GET_PROVIDERS).activities[i].exported/name/permission, getActivityInfo(ComponentName, 0), resolveActivity/queryIntentActivities for the deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock`, ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion/minSdkVersion/flags, ComponentInfo.exported default per targetSdk. Regression: synthetic chain where the boolean comes from ChallengeActivity's exported flag (true) and a decoy non-exported component (false -> -1).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"multidex-class-resolution\", \"concept\": \"multidex APK: classes2.dex..classesN.dex, chain spans dexes, duplicate class defs (first dex wins) (row 107)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every APK so far had one classes.dex; a real dependency surface ships libraries in a secondary dex. Ensure lib.android (puzzle_candidates, deep evaluator, strings scans, proof_flow, callgraph) loads classes.dex, classes2.dex, ... in numeric order (classes10 after classes9, not lexicographic), resolves a class to its FIRST definition (ART/PathClassLoader order), and lets the chain call across dexes (string/type/method ids are per-dex: never share index tables). Also: duplicate class in classes2 with a different ANS- const = decoy. Regression: split a fixture's chain classes across 2 dexes + a shadow copy in classes3.dex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"schema-deescalation-guard\", \"concept\": \"timed schema can go BACK (D27: v2 vanished from TT and all 11 Mastery sets)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D27 was solved 3/3 only because v1 decoders still race first in solve.py. Keep that order: v1 puzzle `data` decode -> split-bundle fill -> v2 evaluator -> code scans; never skip v1 because the day number is >= 23 or because yesterday was v2; regression cases from every schema stay in solver/cases.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-jar-dependency\", \"concept\": \"dependency shipped as JVM bytecode (assets/*.jar, .aar -> classes.jar, *.class), not dex (row 108)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure-python class-