{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A414mC7ijst4QGQr4VDrc7","type":"tool_result","content":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json   (triage.md prints it)\n   v1 {\"codec\":..,\"data\":..} -> python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"; submit ANS-...\n   v2 {\"schema\":\"...v2\",\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..} NO data (D23-D26 + D28 TT+Mastery; D27 all v1) -> COMPUTED:\n   run solve.py / lib.android.puzzle_candidates first (D24, D25: 3/3 modes, <2 s); by hand only if silent: step 5a.\n   *.apks / zip of inner APKs (D26) -> unzip; base = member with huntress_puzzle.json; the OTHER splits hold evidence:\n   v1 feature JSON {part, part_index} fills the empty parts[] slot, then scatter; v2 base dex reads a split asset (5b).\n   Prompt VERBS (\"pinned emulator\", \"forge or replay\", \"prove reachable\", \"reconstruct the protocol\") never meant live work;\n   NOUNS can (D26 \"splits\"). D27 \"dependency flaw\" = base64 JSON; if lib code ships: step 4 dependency line.\n   Never chase 127.0.0.1:19090 (device loopback). Never submit a regex-composed ANS- (hex table + dead mixers = decoys).\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      v1 codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`)? open THAT entry, recurse. int list (D5/D17): r[order[i]]=data[i]\n                                    `packet` (D28): hex -> magic 'HA' | u8 len | payload | XOR8 of all prior bytes; fullmatch the\n                                    PAYLOAD. >1 frame: order by seq, drop replayed nonces + bad checksums, then join\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    D16 gate *_native*(int