dependency` / STRUCTURAL 'reachable challenge-owned dependency' shipped as words only; a regeneration will likely bundle 2+ generated libs. Pure-python `lib.android.dependency_inventory(apk) -> [{pkg, name, version, source, classes, dex}]`: group dex classes by package prefix not under the manifest package (and not android/androidx/kotlin/java), read version from `META-INF/*.version` (androidx style 'x.y.z'), `META-INF/maven/<g>/<a>/pom.properties` (version=), `META-INF/*.kotlin_module`, static final String fields named VERSION/VERSION_NAME/LIB_VERSION in the lib's BuildConfig, `assets/*.jar|*.aar` members (recurse), `lib/<abi>/*.so` version strings\n  {\"id\": \"exported-surface-sink-reachability\", \"concept\": \"several generated dependency flaws; only the one reachable from a manifest-EXPORTED component counts (rows 1, 8, 106)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 prompt: 'Prove which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface'; TT stub `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`. Build on the existing entry-reachable-callgraph-rank, but start from EVERY exported component: parse the binary manifest for activity/activity-alias/service/receiver/provider with exported=true, or an intent-filter and no exported attr when targetSdk<31 (legacy implicit export), minus those guarded by a signature-level permission; entry methods onCreate/onNewIntent/onStartCommand/onBind/onReceive/query/insert/openFile/call/handleMessage. Walk invoke-static/virtual/direct/interface/super (+ reflection name\n  {\"id\": \"v2-boolean-gate-manifest-facts\", \"concept\": \"v2 gate with boolean/narrow args fed by manifest/PackageManager facts (`(ZI)I` exportedReachability; ActivityInfo.exported, permission, targetSdk)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If D27 returns as v2 (TT mutation or Mastery regeneration), the gate is `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1` -- first boolean-typed theme arg. Deep evaluator: correct Z/B/S/C arg + return semantics (if-eqz on Z, int-to-byte/short/char narrowing, boolean returned as int), and intrinsics returning REAL manifest facts: PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_ACTIVITIES|GET_SERVICES|GET_RECEIVERS|GET_PROVIDERS).activities[i].exported/name/permission, getActivityInfo(ComponentName, 0), resolveActivity/queryIntentActivities for the deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock`, ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion/minSdkVersion/flags, Comp\n  {\"id\": \"multidex-class-resolution\", \"concept\": \"multidex APK: classes2.dex..classesN.dex, chain spans dexes, duplicate class defs (first dex wins) (row 107)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every APK so far had one classes.dex; a real dependency surface ships libraries in a secondary dex. Ensure lib.android (puzzle_candidates, deep evaluator, strings scans, proof_flow, callgraph) loads classes.dex, classes2.dex, ... in numeric order (classes10 after classes9, not lexicographic), resolves a class to its FIRST definition (ART/PathClassLoader order), and lets the chain call across dexes (string/type/method ids are per-dex: never share index tables). Also: duplicate class in classes2 with a different ANS- const = decoy. Regression: split a fixture's chain classes across 2 dexes + a shadow copy in classes3.dex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"schema-deescalation-guard\", \"concept\": \"timed schema can go BACK (D27: v2 vanished from TT and all 11 Mastery sets)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D27 was solved 3/3 only because v1 decoders still race first in solve.py. Keep that order: v1 puzzle `data` decode -> split-bundle fill -> v2 evaluator -> code scans; never skip v1 because the day number is >= 23 or because yesterday was v2; regression cases from every schema stay in solver/cases.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-jar-dependency\", \"concept\": \"dependency shipped as JVM bytecode (assets/*.jar, .aar -> classes.jar, *.class), not dex (row 108)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure-python class-file reader: magic CAFEBABE, constant pool (Utf8/Integer/Float/Long/Double/Class/String/Fieldref/Methodref/NameAndType/MethodHandle/InvokeDynamic; Long/Double take 2 slots), fields with ConstantValue attribute (static finals), methods' Code attribute; tiny JVM interpreter for static pure methods (iconst/ldc/ldc2_w/lload/lstore/ladd/lsub/lmul/lxor/lor/land/lshl/lshr/lushr/l2i/i2l/invokestatic/ireturn/lreturn/if*/goto/tableswitch) so a v2-style chain into the jar evaluates. Walk nested zips (aar -> classes.jar -> *.class). Regression: synthetic jar with an ANS- const and a 2-method long chain; `javap -c -constants` (installed) for cross-checking while building only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dependency-version-advisory-match\", \"concept\": \"challenge-owned advisory list matched against bundled lib versions (semver, Maven ordering, lexicographic trap) (row 109)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'generated dependency flaw' suggests a generated advisory table (asset JSON or dex string array: id, package, affected range '<1.2.10', '[1.0,1.3)', fixed version) plus several lib versions. Implement version compare: numeric segments (1.2.10 > 1.2.9), Maven qualifiers (alpha<beta<milestone<rc<snapshot<''<sp), '-SNAPSHOT', 'v' prefix, build metadata '+x' ignored; range syntaxes npm/semver (^ ~ < <= >= ||), Maven interval [a,b), python-style '>=1.0,<2.0'. Return affected (lib, advisory) pairs; combine with exported-surface-sink-reachability to choose the one that is affected AND reachable. Regression: table where a lexicographic compare picks the wrong lib.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deeplink-input-validation-eval\", \"concept\": \"exported deep-link handler validates its input (host/path allowlist, startsWith/endsWith/contains, regex, intent:// parseUri) -- the accepted argument feeds the answer (row 112)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"MASVS-CODE-4 is the natural follow-up to D27's 'exported mobile surface'. Model android.net.Uri semantics in the evaluator: Uri.parse never throws; getHost lowercases? (no: returns as given), getPath percent-decoded, getEncodedPath raw, getQueryParameter decodes %XX and '+' -> ' ' only via UrlQuerySanitizer (Uri keeps '+'), returns FIRST duplicate, getQueryParameters all; getLastPathSegment; Intent.parseUri('intent://...#Intent;scheme=..;S.key=val;end'). For validators with a finite accepted set (string equals, startsWith on a const, regex fullmatch with a literal), derive the accepted value and continue the c\n  {\"id\": \"zip-slip-entry-normalize\", \"concept\": \"archive extraction in a dependency: entries with ../, absolute, backslash or duplicate names; only the entry that resolves to the checked path counts (row 110)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Classic vulnerable-dependency flaw (zip slip, CVE-2018 class). When an APK asset is a zip/jar that the dex extracts (ZipInputStream.getNextEntry + new File(dir, name) + FileOutputStream, or a lib unzip helper), resolve each entry like Java: File(dir,name) concatenation, getCanonicalPath() normalisation of '..' and '.', backslash kept as a literal char on Android, absolute names re-rooted under dir by File(parent, child), later duplicate entries overwrite earlier ones; then answer the dex's read of the target path (e.g. files/config.json or the code-cache dex). Use raw central-directory names (zipfile sanitises) -- read via the existi\n  {\"id\": \"sdk-int-platform-gate\", \"concept\": \"branches on Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion (legacy platform behaviour, implicit export pre-31) (row 111)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'legacy_dependency' hints at legacy-platform behaviour too (MASVS-CODE-1). Evaluator intrinsics: Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / RELEASE / CODENAME from the pinned-emulator profile (keep the value in ONE place with pinned-emulator-env-profile; default API 34, RELEASE '14'), ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion from the APK's own <uses-sdk> (binary manifest), Build.VERSION_CODES constants inlined by javac (sget vs const). Exported default: android:exported absent + intent-filter -> exported iff targetSdk < 31. Regression: a chain that takes a different branch at targetSdk 30 vs 31.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26 repeat: the mastery generalize worker wrote a split-aware eval that never persisted in solve.py. D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"app-update-version-gate\", \"concept\": \"forced-update / minimum-version gate: PackageInfo.versionCode/versionName compared with an asset or dex minimum (MASVS-CODE-2) (row 109)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Supply PackageManager.getPackageInfo(own pkg).versionCode/longVersionCode/versionName from the binary manifest (the fixture has versionCode/versionName attrs), parse the asset's update policy (JSON minVersion/minCode/blocked list), and evaluate the comparison with the same version semantics as dependency-version-advisory-match (reuse it). The answer is the value on the branch the APK's real version takes. Regression: versionName '6.0.1' vs min '6.0.10' (lexicographic trap).\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e22d0874-84fb-4a84-922c-45657a5dacfa","uuid":"9de58666-466e-44de-bf5d-461cf5ad2f8e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:41:02.476Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json   (triage.md prints it)\n   v1 {\"codec\":..,\"data\":..} -> python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"; submit ANS-...\n   v2 {\"schema\":\"...v2\",\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..} NO data (D23-D26 + D28 TT+Mastery; D27 all v1) -> COMPUTED:\n   run solve.py / lib.android.puzzle_candidates first (D24, D25: 3/3 modes, <2 s); by hand only if silent: step 5a.\n   *.apks / zip of inner APKs (D26) -> unzip; base = member with huntress_puzzle.json; the OTHER splits hold evidence:\n   v1 feature JSON {part, part_index} fills the empty parts[] slot, then scatter; v2 base dex reads a split asset (5b).\n   Prompt VERBS (\"pinned emulator\", \"forge or replay\", \"prove reachable\", \"reconstruct the protocol\") never meant live work;\n   NOUNS can (D26 \"splits\"). D27 \"dependency flaw\" = base64 JSON; if lib code ships: step 4 dependency line.\n   Never chase 127.0.0.1:19090 (device loopback). Never submit a regex-composed ANS- (hex table + dead mixers = decoys).\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      v1 codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`)? open THAT entry, recurse. int list (D5/D17): r[order[i]]=data[i]\n                                    `packet` (D28): hex -> magic 'HA' | u8 len | payload | XOR8 of all prior bytes; fullmatch the\n                                    PAYLOAD. >1 frame: order by seq, drop replayed nonces + bad checksums, then join\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    D16 gate *_native*(int): objdump -d (len 65536); v2 nativeShare(long) MID-CHAIN: port/unicorn\n   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob Xamarin XALZ=lz4 -> ilspycmd | global-metadata.dat IL2CPP | assets/www hybrid | Flutter libapp.so\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code (D20 plain dex): strings -a first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> known-\n                                    plaintext unwrap; >1 payload -> host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> member the host names\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml / resources.arsc   aapt dump xmltree ... ; aapt dump --values resources x.apk\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem|*.der  keystore (password = dex string) / attestation cert: openssl x509 -inform DER -text\n   base.apk + feature.apk / split_config.<abi|dpi|lang>.apk / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip,\n                                    list EVERY member; config splits: only the pinned x86_64 / default-dpi / en one counts\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16): for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l vs unzip -l differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest: aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E 'exported|scheme|host|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|\n   usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|meta-data'   (meta-data huntress.mechanic = theme; debuggable D21 = fact only)\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY|CODEC|CONTROL|STRUCTURAL|ANS-' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex      SecretKeySpec/Cipher -> static key decrypt     loadLibrary -> .so\n   Random/setSeed -> regenerate RNG                MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash                   Binder/onReceive -> IPC\n   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/debuggerGate/rootSignals/hook_detection -> clean_device_scan, clean value PER\n   signal; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag. Class.forName -> reflection_scan. $SwitchMap$ /\n   packed-switch loop -> flattened_cfg_scan. CertificatePinner -> pins. KeyStore BKS/PKCS12 -> res/raw keystore.\n   Dependency (D27 theme): lib pkgs / classes2.dex / assets/*.jar / pom.properties -> inventory; the value counts only\n   if reached from a manifest-EXPORTED component (exported=true or intent-filter); other libs' flaws are decoys.\n5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   Old-day v2 sets run their REAL mechanic: d19 forName(\"m\"+dispatch(k)).invoke -> only that Maze.mN; d16 (u16)len gate\n   -> the dex's own int arg; d18 decrypt loop; d17 a.b->a.a. D28 TT: int[8] next/val tables walked 7 rounds, keep order.\n5b. Split-reading chain (D26): base dex `readSplit(name)` walks ctx.getApplicationInfo().splitSourceDirs + ZipFile\n   getEntry(\"assets/\"+name) -> 16 B -> two big-endian u64 (`j=(j<<8)|(b[i]&255)`). Serve `unzip -p feature.apk\n   assets/<name>` to the port / javac stub. Split with hasCode=true -> jadx its dex too and javac all together.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23-D26 v2, D27 v1, D28 v2; 12 sets); each APK alone;\n   loop all answer_ids; one silent set -> hand-solve it, but batch-submit every answer in one request.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain,\nanalysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening, analysis-interface-signal-list-eval, analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs,\nanalysis-release-code-eval, analysis-self-integrity-stubs, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\nanti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload, apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbiometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, bundle-container-formats, cdex-vdex-string-pool,\ncert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs,\ncustom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel,\ndecrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-eval-float-double-semantics, dex-eval-java-random-lcg,\ndex-eval-long-intrinsics, dex-eval-native-bridge, dex-eval-pure-static-memo, dex-gated-branch-consts,\ndex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays,\ndispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-anchored-candidate-veto, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\nenum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table,\nhook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\ninstaller-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, instrumentation-false-positive-env, integrity-derived-key,\njanus-dex-apk-polyglot, java-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input,\njni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify, key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse,\nknown-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, kotlin-object-chain-eval,\nmastery-set-scaling-bench, messagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native,\nmulti-stage-loader-recurse, native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks, native-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt,\nnative-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate, native-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export,\nnative-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs, nested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch,\npayload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family,\npinned-emulator-env-profile, play-integrity-verdict-select, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields,\nr8-renamed-chain-follow, reflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve,\nrolling-xor-keystream-family, root-signal-vector-key, split-config-device-select, split-feature-dex-code,\nsplit-native-lib-config-abi, split-resources-arsc-overlay, split-signature-digest-binding, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt,\nstatic-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan,\nv1-manifest-digest-verify, v2-app-state-first-run-defaults, v2-debugger-gate-state-loop, v2-dexloader-payload-invoke,\nv2-reflection-api-breadth, v2-split-asset-read, v2-string-decrypt-name-resolve, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\n\nForecast after D27: D26's packaging turn did NOT continue -- D27 \"Dependency Surface\" (MASVS-CODE-3 software\ncomposition: \"which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface\") shipped NOTHING real: v1\n`base64` in single + TT, and all 11 Mastery sets went back to v1 with their original codecs (v2 absent after 4 days).\nSo (a) a TT/Mastery regeneration of D27 as v2 or as real bundled-library code is the likeliest near-term mutation\n(priority 1: dependency inventory, exported-surface -> lib-sink reachability, multidex, a `(ZI)I` gate fed by manifest\nfacts); (b) the MASVS-CODE group is now open: CODE-4 input validation (deep-link parse/allowlist bypass, zip slip in a\ndependency, deserialization), CODE-1 platform version gates, CODE-2 forced update (priority 2); (c) still unnamed for\nD28-D31 (4 days): certificate pinning, key attestation, tamper/repackaging, task hijacking/tapjacking, the obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and an all-days capstone. Mastery: 11 sets on D27 (+1/day -> ~15 by D31), schema\nper set unpredictable (v1 or v2); keep v1 decoders first in the race, v2 evaluator always armed. Old days not yet seen\nas v2: d05, d08, d12, d18, d20, d27.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"dependency-sbom-inventory\", \"concept\": \"bundled third-party dependency inventory (rows 106-108): library packages outside the app package, versions and their source\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 theme `legacy_dependency` / STRUCTURAL 'reachable challenge-owned dependency' shipped as words only; a regeneration will likely bundle 2+ generated libs. Pure-python `lib.android.dependency_inventory(apk) -> [{pkg, name, version, source, classes, dex}]`: group dex classes by package prefix not under the manifest package (and not android/androidx/kotlin/java), read version from `META-INF/*.version` (androidx style 'x.y.z'), `META-INF/maven/<g>/<a>/pom.properties` (version=), `META-INF/*.kotlin_module`, static final String fields named VERSION/VERSION_NAME/LIB_VERSION in the lib's BuildConfig, `assets/*.jar|*.aar` members (recurse), `lib/<abi>/*.so` version strings\n  {\"id\": \"exported-surface-sink-reachability\", \"concept\": \"several generated dependency flaws; only the one reachable from a manifest-EXPORTED component counts (rows 1, 8, 106)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 prompt: 'Prove which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface'; TT stub `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`. Build on the existing entry-reachable-callgraph-rank, but start from EVERY exported component: parse the binary manifest for activity/activity-alias/service/receiver/provider with exported=true, or an intent-filter and no exported attr when targetSdk<31 (legacy implicit export), minus those guarded by a signature-level permission; entry methods onCreate/onNewIntent/onStartCommand/onBind/onReceive/query/insert/openFile/call/handleMessage. Walk invoke-static/virtual/direct/interface/super (+ reflection name\n  {\"id\": \"v2-boolean-gate-manifest-facts\", \"concept\": \"v2 gate with boolean/narrow args fed by manifest/PackageManager facts (`(ZI)I` exportedReachability; ActivityInfo.exported, permission, targetSdk)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If D27 returns as v2 (TT mutation or Mastery regeneration), the gate is `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1` -- first boolean-typed theme arg. Deep evaluator: correct Z/B/S/C arg + return semantics (if-eqz on Z, int-to-byte/short/char narrowing, boolean returned as int), and intrinsics returning REAL manifest facts: PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_ACTIVITIES|GET_SERVICES|GET_RECEIVERS|GET_PROVIDERS).activities[i].exported/name/permission, getActivityInfo(ComponentName, 0), resolveActivity/queryIntentActivities for the deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock`, ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion/minSdkVersion/flags, Comp\n  {\"id\": \"multidex-class-resolution\", \"concept\": \"multidex APK: classes2.dex..classesN.dex, chain spans dexes, duplicate class defs (first dex wins) (row 107)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every APK so far had one classes.dex; a real dependency surface ships libraries in a secondary dex. Ensure lib.android (puzzle_candidates, deep evaluator, strings scans, proof_flow, callgraph) loads classes.dex, classes2.dex, ... in numeric order (classes10 after classes9, not lexicographic), resolves a class to its FIRST definition (ART/PathClassLoader order), and lets the chain call across dexes (string/type/method ids are per-dex: never share index tables). Also: duplicate class in classes2 with a different ANS- const = decoy. Regression: split a fixture's chain classes across 2 dexes + a shadow copy in classes3.dex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"schema-deescalation-guard\", \"concept\": \"timed schema can go BACK (D27: v2 vanished from TT and all 11 Mastery sets)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D27 was solved 3/3 only because v1 decoders still race first in solve.py. Keep that order: v1 puzzle `data` decode -> split-bundle fill -> v2 evaluator -> code scans; never skip v1 because the day number is >= 23 or because yesterday was v2; regression cases from every schema stay in solver/cases.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-jar-dependency\", \"concept\": \"dependency shipped as JVM bytecode (assets/*.jar, .aar -> classes.jar, *.class), not dex (row 108)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure-python class-file reader: magic CAFEBABE, constant pool (Utf8/Integer/Float/Long/Double/Class/String/Fieldref/Methodref/NameAndType/MethodHandle/InvokeDynamic; Long/Double take 2 slots), fields with ConstantValue attribute (static finals), methods' Code attribute; tiny JVM interpreter for static pure methods (iconst/ldc/ldc2_w/lload/lstore/ladd/lsub/lmul/lxor/lor/land/lshl/lshr/lushr/l2i/i2l/invokestatic/ireturn/lreturn/if*/goto/tableswitch) so a v2-style chain into the jar evaluates. Walk nested zips (aar -> classes.jar -> *.class). Regression: synthetic jar with an ANS- const and a 2-method long chain; `javap -c -constants` (installed) for cross-checking while building only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dependency-version-advisory-match\", \"concept\": \"challenge-owned advisory list matched against bundled lib versions (semver, Maven ordering, lexicographic trap) (row 109)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'generated dependency flaw' suggests a generated advisory table (asset JSON or dex string array: id, package, affected range '<1.2.10', '[1.0,1.3)', fixed version) plus several lib versions. Implement version compare: numeric segments (1.2.10 > 1.2.9), Maven qualifiers (alpha<beta<milestone<rc<snapshot<''<sp), '-SNAPSHOT', 'v' prefix, build metadata '+x' ignored; range syntaxes npm/semver (^ ~ < <= >= ||), Maven interval [a,b), python-style '>=1.0,<2.0'. Return affected (lib, advisory) pairs; combine with exported-surface-sink-reachability to choose the one that is affected AND reachable. Regression: table where a lexicographic compare picks the wrong lib.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deeplink-input-validation-eval\", \"concept\": \"exported deep-link handler validates its input (host/path allowlist, startsWith/endsWith/contains, regex, intent:// parseUri) -- the accepted argument feeds the answer (row 112)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"MASVS-CODE-4 is the natural follow-up to D27's 'exported mobile surface'. Model android.net.Uri semantics in the evaluator: Uri.parse never throws; getHost lowercases? (no: returns as given), getPath percent-decoded, getEncodedPath raw, getQueryParameter decodes %XX and '+' -> ' ' only via UrlQuerySanitizer (Uri keeps '+'), returns FIRST duplicate, getQueryParameters all; getLastPathSegment; Intent.parseUri('intent://...#Intent;scheme=..;S.key=val;end'). For validators with a finite accepted set (string equals, startsWith on a const, regex fullmatch with a literal), derive the accepted value and continue the c\n  {\"id\": \"zip-slip-entry-normalize\", \"concept\": \"archive extraction in a dependency: entries with ../, absolute, backslash or duplicate names; only the entry that resolves to the checked path counts (row 110)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Classic vulnerable-dependency flaw (zip slip, CVE-2018 class). When an APK asset is a zip/jar that the dex extracts (ZipInputStream.getNextEntry + new File(dir, name) + FileOutputStream, or a lib unzip helper), resolve each entry like Java: File(dir,name) concatenation, getCanonicalPath() normalisation of '..' and '.', backslash kept as a literal char on Android, absolute names re-rooted under dir by File(parent, child), later duplicate entries overwrite earlier ones; then answer the dex's read of the target path (e.g. files/config.json or the code-cache dex). Use raw central-directory names (zipfile sanitises) -- read via the existi\n  {\"id\": \"sdk-int-platform-gate\", \"concept\": \"branches on Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion (legacy platform behaviour, implicit export pre-31) (row 111)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'legacy_dependency' hints at legacy-platform behaviour too (MASVS-CODE-1). Evaluator intrinsics: Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / RELEASE / CODENAME from the pinned-emulator profile (keep the value in ONE place with pinned-emulator-env-profile; default API 34, RELEASE '14'), ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion from the APK's own <uses-sdk> (binary manifest), Build.VERSION_CODES constants inlined by javac (sget vs const). Exported default: android:exported absent + intent-filter -> exported iff targetSdk < 31. Regression: a chain that takes a different branch at targetSdk 30 vs 31.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26 repeat: the mastery generalize worker wrote a split-aware eval that never persisted in solve.py. D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"app-update-version-gate\", \"concept\": \"forced-update / minimum-version gate: PackageInfo.versionCode/versionName compared with an asset or dex minimum (MASVS-CODE-2) (row 109)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Supply PackageManager.getPackageInfo(own pkg).versionCode/longVersionCode/versionName from the binary manifest (the fixture has versionCode/versionName attrs), parse the asset's update policy (JSON minVersion/minCode/blocked list), and evaluate the comparison with the same version semantics as dependency-version-advisory-match (reuse it). The answer is the value on the branch the APK's real version takes. Regression: versionName '6.0.1' vs min '6.0.10' (lexicographic trap).\"}\n]\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A414mC7ijst4QGQr4VDrc7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
