{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZdG38ZWbetcSw1H4anc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QGCA2EDusf8iwYEczL5DXQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,textwrap\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndone=sorted(k.split(':',1)[1] for k,v in st.items() if k.startswith('mobile-android:') and (v.get('ok') or (v.get('attempts') or 0)>=2))\na=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nj0=s.index('```json',a); j1=s.index('```',j0+7)\nold=json.loads(s[j0+7:j1])\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in old if g['id'] not in done}\nprint('kept', list(keep))\nhead=(\"## Readiness gaps\\n\\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \\\"prebuild\\\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\\n\"\n\"`solve.py`. \\\"tool\\\" = install. \\\"note\\\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\\n\")\nhead+=\"\\n\".join(textwrap.wrap(\", \".join(done)+\".\", 118))+\"\\n\\n\"\nfc=\"\"\"Forecast after D30 (D31 = the LAST day): D28-D30 each shipped a NEW v1 codec that is a small STACK of known steps\n(`packet` hex+frame+XOR8, `table` hex+`b-(key+3i)`, `layered` base64+`b^(key+i)`+reverse) and a v2 TT gate that encodes\nthe same idea; prompts list far more than ships (D30: \"obfuscation, native indirection, runtime decryption, integrity\nchecks\" -> one peel fn). D30's race probe was SILENT on `layered` (LLM 40 s): a generic stacked-codec search is the top\ngap. For the finale expect (a) a v1 codec stacking 3-4 steps or declaring `layers`/`steps`, possibly any older codec;\n(b) a v2 chain that finally COMPOSES old mechanics in one build (JNI hop + decrypt loop + reflection + split read +\nCRC/digest \"integrity\"); (c) a 15-set Mastery from any day in either schema (d12, d20, d27 never yet v2). Words that have\nnever turned real and could on a capstone: d28 multi-frame seq/nonce, d27 bundled-lib reachability, d29 AES T-boxes.\n\n\"\"\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"v1-composed-codec-search\",\"concept\":\"composed / stacked v1 codec: 2-4 known steps under one unknown codec name and one int `key` (row 118, row 70)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 `layered` = base64 -> b ^ ((key+i)&255) -> reverse; D29 `table` = hex -> (b - (key+3i)) & 255; the D30 race probe was silent (each step exists in lib.android, the STACK did not). Add `lib.android.stacked_codec_search(puzzle)`: unwrap {hex, base64 (std/urlsafe, padding-tolerant), base32, base85/a85, none}; then try keystream ops {xor, sub, add} with streams key+c*i (c in -7..7), key^i, (key*i)&255, key-cycled bytes of str(key)/key.to_bytes, prev-byte chaining (b ^ prev), and caesar on chars; plus reverse/byte-swap pairs/nibble-swap before or after each step; depth <= 4, prune by printable-ASCII after the keystream step; accept only a fullmatch of ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ and require a UNIQUE result (else return all to the ranker). Shortcut: fit c from the per-position deltas against b'ANS-' at index 0 and against the reversed tail. Must run < 50 ms. Regression: the D29 and D30 singles + synthetic stacks (b85 -> add key+2i -> reverse; hex -> xor key^i -> base64 inner).\"},\n {\"id\":\"v1-declared-layers-pipeline\",\"concept\":\"puzzle JSON that DECLARES its pipeline (`layers`/`steps`/`pipeline`/`chain` list, per-step keys, nested puzzle JSON inside decoded data)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Finale form of D30: {\\\"codec\\\":\\\"layered\\\",\\\"layers\\\":[\\\"base64\\\",{\\\"xor\\\":12,\\\"step\\\":1},\\\"reverse\\\"]} or keys key/key2/iv/step/offset, or a decoded payload that is itself a huntress puzzle JSON (onion). Implement a step registry reusing every v1 codec seen d1-d30 (plain, reverse, base64, hex, xor, caesar, split+order, indexed, packet, table, layered, dynamic entry path) with its params, apply the declared list in order (also try reversed order when the forward order fails), recurse into decoded JSON up to depth 5, and fall back to v1-composed-codec-search on an unknown step name. Regression: synthetic 3-step and nested-onion puzzles.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-composed-mechanics-chain\",\"concept\":\"one v2 build composing several old mechanics in sequence (row 119)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 prompt promised native indirection + runtime decryption + integrity checks; the TT shipped only peelStack. A capstone build may chain: JNI nativeShare(long[,int]) (d15/d16) -> decryptByte loop over a byte[] (d18) -> Class.forName(decrypted name).getDeclaredMethod(\\\"m\\\"+dispatch(k)).invoke (d19) -> readSplit/getAssets bytes (d26) -> CRC32/MessageDigest over own asset/dex bytes (d25) -> state-machine walk (d28) -> table walk (d29) -> peel (d30). Build a synthetic fixture (javac + d8 offline at prebuild time only) whose token() goes through ALL of these in one dex + libarena.so + an .apks wrapper, and make lib's deep evaluator + solve.py _native_eval solve it end-to-end in < 1 s; also verify a decrypted string feeding forName is resolved before dispatch.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-checksum-intrinsics-crc32-adler\",\"concept\":\"'integrity checks' made real in the v2 chain: java.util.zip.CRC32/Adler32/Checksum, MessageDigest over the APK's own bytes (asset, classes.dex, signing cert)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Evaluator intrinsics: CRC32()/Adler32() update(int)/update(byte[],off,len)/getValue (unsigned 32-bit in a long), MessageDigest SHA-1/SHA-256/MD5 digest() -> byte[] then folded big-endian, Arrays.hashCode/String.hashCode, ByteBuffer.wrap(..).getLong/order(LITTLE_ENDIAN); byte sources: getAssets().open(name) / ZipFile entries of the delivered APK, getPackageInfo(GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures[0].toByteArray() = the DER cert from META-INF/*.RSA. Regression: a chain folding CRC32(classes.dex) and SHA-256(cert) into token().\"},\n {\"id\":\"v1-codec-registry-all-days-regression\",\"concept\":\"finale single may reuse ANY v1 codec of d1-d30 (or a stack of them)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Make one table-driven regression over every v1 codec shape seen (plain, reverse, base64, hex, xor b64+key, caesar +/-, split parts+order with empty slot, indexed (3+7i)%20, native/reflection plaintext, dynamic entry path, packet frame, table, layered) with re-rolled keys, and assert solve.py's single path resolves each in the race probe (< 0.2 s) -- D30 showed a codec family the probe did not know costs ~35 s of LLM time.\"},\n {\"id\":\"packet-frame-codec-family\",\"concept\":\"framed binary codec mutations (row 113): u16 length, CRC16/CRC32 instead of XOR8, xored/encoded payload, TLV fields\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 `packet` was solved by hex + ANS- substring search only. Parse explicitly: fixed 2-byte magic (`HA` seen), length u8/u16 BE/LE/varint, payload, checksum XOR8 / sum8 / CRC16-CCITT / CRC32 over header+payload or payload only; payload may itself be xor/base64-encoded (then v1-composed-codec-search). Fullmatch the PAYLOAD; reject frames with a bad checksum.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-frame-seq-nonce-reorder\",\"concept\":\"several frames with seq/nonce fields: out of order, replayed duplicate, stale nonce, bad-checksum decoy (row 114)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 prompt 'preserve nonce and ordering semantics' never turned real; a capstone could. Split a blob into magic-prefixed frames, read seq (u8/u16) and nonce fields, drop bad-checksum frames and repeated nonces (keep the first), order by seq, join payload pieces, fullmatch. Regression: 4-frame blob with one replay and one corrupt frame.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-string-return-to-reflection\",\"concept\":\"native method returns a runtime-decrypted jstring that names the Java method/class to reflect into ('native indirection' + 'runtime decryption')\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Emulate the JNI export in unicorn with a NewStringUTF hook (capture the C string built from an xor-decrypted stack buffer), return it to the dex evaluator as a java String, then resolve Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod with it and invoke only that target; the other same-shape methods are decoys. Regression: libarena.so export decrypting 'm5' and a Maze class with 8 mN.\"},\n {\"id\":\"puzzle-key-from-variant-identity\",\"concept\":\"codec key/seed derived from the per-variant identity (v2 `build`, package suffix v<12 hex>, case ref MOB-NN-<10 hex>, client_secret) instead of a JSON `key`\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"So far the identity never fed the answer. If a v1 puzzle drops `key` or a v2 seed reads the asset `build`, try keys int(build[:2],16), int(build,16)&0xff, sum/xor of identity bytes, the package suffix bytes, String.hashCode of the case ref; always anchored on the ANS- fullmatch. Read build/package/case ref from the APK (JSON, manifest, dex strings), never from the contract text alone.\"},\n {\"id\":\"request-signing-canonical-reconstruct\",\"concept\":\"app-to-backend request signature (canonical string + HMAC/nonce/timestamp headers) computed statically (row 115)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the capstone makes 'proving the same backend effect' real: evaluate Mac.getInstance(HmacSHA256/HmacSHA1).init(SecretKeySpec(key)).doFinal(canonical.getBytes(UTF_8)) and Base64/hex encodings in the evaluator; canonical = method + path + sorted query + nonce + timestamp as built by StringBuilder in the dex; timestamp/nonce from consts. Regression: chain whose token is the first 8 bytes of an HMAC.\"},\n {\"id\":\"rpc-stream-frame-decode\",\"concept\":\"streaming/RPC wire formats in an asset or `data` (gRPC 5-byte prefix + protobuf, WebSocket frame + mask, MQTT varint, SLIP/COBS) (row 116)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure-python decoders: gRPC [flag u8][len u32 BE][protobuf] (reuse protobuf-asset-wire-decode), WebSocket opcode/mask/payload-len 7/16/64 + 4-byte mask xor, MQTT remaining-length varint, SLIP 0xC0/0xDB escapes, COBS. Hook into the v1 race after hex/base64 unwrap.\"},\n {\"id\":\"race-probe-silent-codec-cue\",\"concept\":\"route a silent race probe on an unknown v1 codec straight to the both-ends ANS- fit\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D30: probe silent on `layered`, LLM worker needed ~40 s (decoded base64, then found key+i xor with `-SNA` at the tail). The cue is now in Recognition cues step 1; keep it in the single-solve prompt and in triage.md's 'what the description suggests' when the codec name is unseen.\"},\n]\ngaps=new+list(keep.values())\nids=[g['id'] for g in gaps]\nassert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nfor g in new:\n    assert 'mobile-android:'+g['id'] not in st, g['id']\nbody=head+fc+\"```json\\n[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n```\\n\"\ns=s[:a]+body+s[j1+4:].lstrip('\\n')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\njson.loads(s[s.index('```json')+7:s.rindex('```')])\nprint(len(gaps), sum(1 for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild'))\nEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/mobile-android.md; wc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":991,"cache_read_input_tokens":126019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":991},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e22d0874-84fb-4a84-922c-45657a5dacfa","uuid":"0c33e2e3-8a21-4c80-91ee-c82e8c34a300","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:45:22.548Z","request_id":"req_011CgZdG2uvCDn1nsuqCUGsf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QGCA2EDusf8iwYEczL5DXQ":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,textwrap\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndone=sorted(k.split(':',1)[1] for k,v in st.items() if k.startswith('mobile-android:') and (v.get('ok') or (v.get('attempts') or 0)>=2))\na=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nj0=s.index('```json',a); j1=s.index('```',j0+7)\nold=json.loads(s[j0+7:j1])\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in old if g['id'] not in done}\nprint('kept', list(keep))\nhead=(\"## Readiness gaps\\n\\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \\\"prebuild\\\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\\n\"\n\"`solve.py`. \\\"tool\\\" = install. \\\"note\\\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\\n\")\nhead+=\"\\n\".join(textwrap.wrap(\", \".join(done)+\".\", 118))+\"\\n\\n\"\nfc=\"\"\"Forecast after D30 (D31 = the LAST day): D28-D30 each shipped a NEW v1 codec that is a small STACK of known steps\n(`packet` hex+frame+XOR8, `table` hex+`b-(key+3i)`, `layered` base64+`b^(key+i)`+reverse) and a v2 TT gate that encodes\nthe same idea; prompts list far more than ships (D30: \"obfuscation, native indirection, runtime decryption, integrity\nchecks\" -> one peel fn). D30's race probe was SILENT on `layered` (LLM 40 s): a generic stacked-codec search is the top\ngap. For the finale expect (a) a v1 codec stacking 3-4 steps or declaring `layers`/`steps`, possibly any older codec;\n(b) a v2 chain that finally COMPOSES old mechanics in one build (JNI hop + decrypt loop + reflection + split read +\nCRC/digest \"integrity\"); (c) a 15-set Mastery from any day in either schema (d12, d20, d27 never yet v2). Words that have\nnever turned real and could on a capstone: d28 multi-frame seq/nonce, d27 bundled-lib reachability, d29 AES T-boxes.\n\n\"\"\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"v1-composed-codec-search\",\"concept\":\"composed / stacked v1 codec: 2-4 known steps under one unknown codec name and one int `key` (row 118, row 70)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 `layered` = base64 -> b ^ ((key+i)&255) -> reverse; D29 `table` = hex -> (b - (key+3i)) & 255; the D30 race probe was silent (each step exists in lib.android, the STACK did not). Add `lib.android.stacked_codec_search(puzzle)`: unwrap {hex, base64 (std/urlsafe, padding-tolerant), base32, base85/a85, none}; then try keystream ops {xor, sub, add} with streams key+c*i (c in -7..7), key^i, (key*i)&255, key-cycled bytes of str(key)/key.to_bytes, prev-byte chaining (b ^ prev), and caesar on chars; plus reverse/byte-swap pairs/nibble-swap before or after each step; depth <= 4, prune by printable-ASCII after the keystream step; accept only a fullmatch of ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ and require a UNIQUE result (else return all to the ranker). Shortcut: fit c from the per-position deltas against b'ANS-' at index 0 and against the reversed tail. Must run < 50 ms. Regression: the D29 and D30 singles + synthetic stacks (b85 -> add key+2i -> reverse; hex -> xor key^i -> base64 inner).\"},\n {\"id\":\"v1-declared-layers-pipeline\",\"concept\":\"puzzle JSON that DECLARES its pipeline (`layers`/`steps`/`pipeline`/`chain` list, per-step keys, nested puzzle JSON inside decoded data)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Finale form of D30: {\\\"codec\\\":\\\"layered\\\",\\\"layers\\\":[\\\"base64\\\",{\\\"xor\\\":12,\\\"step\\\":1},\\\"reverse\\\"]} or keys key/key2/iv/step/offset, or a decoded payload that is itself a huntress puzzle JSON (onion). Implement a step registry reusing every v1 codec seen d1-d30 (plain, reverse, base64, hex, xor, caesar, split+order, indexed, packet, table, layered, dynamic entry path) with its params, apply the declared list in order (also try reversed order when the forward order fails), recurse into decoded JSON up to depth 5, and fall back to v1-composed-codec-search on an unknown step name. Regression: synthetic 3-step and nested-onion puzzles.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-composed-mechanics-chain\",\"concept\":\"one v2 build composing several old mechanics in sequence (row 119)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 prompt promised native indirection + runtime decryption + integrity checks; the TT shipped only peelStack. A capstone build may chain: JNI nativeShare(long[,int]) (d15/d16) -> decryptByte loop over a byte[] (d18) -> Class.forName(decrypted name).getDeclaredMethod(\\\"m\\\"+dispatch(k)).invoke (d19) -> readSplit/getAssets bytes (d26) -> CRC32/MessageDigest over own asset/dex bytes (d25) -> state-machine walk (d28) -> table walk (d29) -> peel (d30). Build a synthetic fixture (javac + d8 offline at prebuild time only) whose token() goes through ALL of these in one dex + libarena.so + an .apks wrapper, and make lib's deep evaluator + solve.py _native_eval solve it end-to-end in < 1 s; also verify a decrypted string feeding forName is resolved before dispatch.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-checksum-intrinsics-crc32-adler\",\"concept\":\"'integrity checks' made real in the v2 chain: java.util.zip.CRC32/Adler32/Checksum, MessageDigest over the APK's own bytes (asset, classes.dex, signing cert)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Evaluator intrinsics: CRC32()/Adler32() update(int)/update(byte[],off,len)/getValue (unsigned 32-bit in a long), MessageDigest SHA-1/SHA-256/MD5 digest() -> byte[] then folded big-endian, Arrays.hashCode/String.hashCode, ByteBuffer.wrap(..).getLong/order(LITTLE_ENDIAN); byte sources: getAssets().open(name) / ZipFile entries of the delivered APK, getPackageInfo(GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures[0].toByteArray() = the DER cert from META-INF/*.RSA. Regression: a chain folding CRC32(classes.dex) and SHA-256(cert) into token().\"},\n {\"id\":\"v1-codec-registry-all-days-regression\",\"concept\":\"finale single may reuse ANY v1 codec of d1-d30 (or a stack of them)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Make one table-driven regression over every v1 codec shape seen (plain, reverse, base64, hex, xor b64+key, caesar +/-, split parts+order with empty slot, indexed (3+7i)%20, native/reflection plaintext, dynamic entry path, packet frame, table, layered) with re-rolled keys, and assert solve.py's single path resolves each in the race probe (< 0.2 s) -- D30 showed a codec family the probe did not know costs ~35 s of LLM time.\"},\n {\"id\":\"packet-frame-codec-family\",\"concept\":\"framed binary codec mutations (row 113): u16 length, CRC16/CRC32 instead of XOR8, xored/encoded payload, TLV fields\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 `packet` was solved by hex + ANS- substring search only. Parse explicitly: fixed 2-byte magic (`HA` seen), length u8/u16 BE/LE/varint, payload, checksum XOR8 / sum8 / CRC16-CCITT / CRC32 over header+payload or payload only; payload may itself be xor/base64-encoded (then v1-composed-codec-search). Fullmatch the PAYLOAD; reject frames with a bad checksum.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-frame-seq-nonce-reorder\",\"concept\":\"several frames with seq/nonce fields: out of order, replayed duplicate, stale nonce, bad-checksum decoy (row 114)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 prompt 'preserve nonce and ordering semantics' never turned real; a capstone could. Split a blob into magic-prefixed frames, read seq (u8/u16) and nonce fields, drop bad-checksum frames and repeated nonces (keep the first), order by seq, join payload pieces, fullmatch. Regression: 4-frame blob with one replay and one corrupt frame.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-string-return-to-reflection\",\"concept\":\"native method returns a runtime-decrypted jstring that names the Java method/class to reflect into ('native indirection' + 'runtime decryption')\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Emulate the JNI export in unicorn with a NewStringUTF hook (capture the C string built from an xor-decrypted stack buffer), return it to the dex evaluator as a java String, then resolve Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod with it and invoke only that target; the other same-shape methods are decoys. Regression: libarena.so export decrypting 'm5' and a Maze class with 8 mN.\"},\n {\"id\":\"puzzle-key-from-variant-identity\",\"concept\":\"codec key/seed derived from the per-variant identity (v2 `build`, package suffix v<12 hex>, case ref MOB-NN-<10 hex>, client_secret) instead of a JSON `key`\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"So far the identity never fed the answer. If a v1 puzzle drops `key` or a v2 seed reads the asset `build`, try keys int(build[:2],16), int(build,16)&0xff, sum/xor of identity bytes, the package suffix bytes, String.hashCode of the case ref; always anchored on the ANS- fullmatch. Read build/package/case ref from the APK (JSON, manifest, dex strings), never from the contract text alone.\"},\n {\"id\":\"request-signing-canonical-reconstruct\",\"concept\":\"app-to-backend request signature (canonical string + HMAC/nonce/timestamp headers) computed statically (row 115)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the capstone makes 'proving the same backend effect' real: evaluate Mac.getInstance(HmacSHA256/HmacSHA1).init(SecretKeySpec(key)).doFinal(canonical.getBytes(UTF_8)) and Base64/hex encodings in the evaluator; canonical = method + path + sorted query + nonce + timestamp as built by StringBuilder in the dex; timestamp/nonce from consts. Regression: chain whose token is the first 8 bytes of an HMAC.\"},\n {\"id\":\"rpc-stream-frame-decode\",\"concept\":\"streaming/RPC wire formats in an asset or `data` (gRPC 5-byte prefix + protobuf, WebSocket frame + mask, MQTT varint, SLIP/COBS) (row 116)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure-python decoders: gRPC [flag u8][len u32 BE][protobuf] (reuse protobuf-asset-wire-decode), WebSocket opcode/mask/payload-len 7/16/64 + 4-byte mask xor, MQTT remaining-length varint, SLIP 0xC0/0xDB escapes, COBS. Hook into the v1 race after hex/base64 unwrap.\"},\n {\"id\":\"race-probe-silent-codec-cue\",\"concept\":\"route a silent race probe on an unknown v1 codec straight to the both-ends ANS- fit\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D30: probe silent on `layered`, LLM worker needed ~40 s (decoded base64, then found key+i xor with `-SNA` at the tail). The cue is now in Recognition cues step 1; keep it in the single-solve prompt and in triage.md's 'what the description suggests' when the codec name is unseen.\"},\n]\ngaps=new+list(keep.values())\nids=[g['id'] for g in gaps]\nassert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nfor g in new:\n    assert 'mobile-android:'+g['id'] not in st, g['id']\nbody=head+fc+\"```json\\n[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n```\\n\"\ns=s[:a]+body+s[j1+4:].lstrip('\\n')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\njson.loads(s[s.index('```json')+7:s.rindex('```')])\nprint(len(gaps), sum(1 for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild'))\nEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/mobile-android.md; wc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"}}}
